    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "reasoning": "The student identifies the religious aspect but struggles to articulate the concept of 'certainty' in the context of the novel's themes of social decay and personal crisis. I will provide a brief, direct explanation of how his faith acts as an anchor, then ask them to synthesize this into a final answer.",
      "content": "It is understandable to feel stuck there. In the novel, Kumalo faces a world that is falling apart—his son is lost, his community is broken, and his traditions are fading. When he refers to 'this' as 'certain,' he is contrasting the chaos of his surroundings with the stability of his faith. The Bible and his belief system are the only constants that do not change, even when everything else does. \n\nGiven that, how would you phrase the final answer to show that his faith provides both comfort and stability?"
    },
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "So, it's because his faith and the Bible are the only things that give him comfort and keep him steady when everything else is uncertain."
